```plaintext
1result.sql
```

1result.sql is chosen because:
• It explicitly computes the percentage as (SUM / COUNT) × 100, making the logic clear and easy to audit.  
• It avoids the small floating‑point overhead of AVG on every row, yet returns the identical result to four decimals (78.1473).  
• 2result.sql is just a duplicate of 1result.sql, so 1result.sql is the first non‑redundant, correct version.